cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use VERB, cite it as below. Measured verification costs are more welcome than citations."
title: "VERB: The Verification Budget"
abstract: >-
  An operating model for autonomous AI in project delivery and end to end PMO.
  Core claim: AI agents in project management are no longer constrained by model
  capability but by verification bandwidth, meaning how many agent decisions an
  organisation can genuinely review before review becomes rubber-stamping. The
  repository contains the specification, the verification budget formula
  VB = (R x H x u) / c, the A/B/C/D decision classes, the agent role contract,
  the evidence plane, six operating metrics including silent drift, four eval
  gates, maturity stages S0 to S4, JSON schemas, a Python reference
  implementation and a static calculator.
type: software
